<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37867" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαθλον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prize of a contest,</i> mostly in
			pl., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				52
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἔ. τοῦ πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Flam.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			; <i>rewards,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					28.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				455.3
			</span></i> (Aphrodisias, M.Antonius), <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				1.17.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἐπὶ σαφέσι τοῖς
			ἐ.</span> not even if the <i>advantages</i> (of taking an
			emetic) were obvious, <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				8.23.2
			</span></i>: also in sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοὺς ἑκάστῳ τὸ ὑπὲρ τῆς φιλοπονίας
					ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Prien.</u>
					113.31
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτιθεμένου ἐ. τῷ λύσαντι γαμεῖν τὴν
					Ἰοκάστην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					4.64
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			.</div>
